<overview>
<p>Conventional infantry within the FWLM serve as the backbone of provincial defense across a patchwork of semi-autonomous states, each maintaining its own military traditions and equipment preferences. Towing crew-served gauss rifles, these platoons field the most advanced ballistic direct-fire weapon available to conventional infantry. Magnetic acceleration delivers projectiles at extreme velocities with no recoil signature, though the weapon's power requirements and fragility demand careful handling.</p>
</overview>

<notes>
Intro date based on re-introduction date of Gauss Rifle
</notes>

